       Earlier  System  V  curses implementations specified that with ssccrroollllookk
       enabled, any window modification triggering  a  scroll  also  forced  a
       physical  refresh.   X/Open  Curses  does not require this, and _n_c_u_r_s_e_s
       avoids doing it to perform better vertical-motion optimization at  wwrree‐‐
       ffrreesshh time.

       X/Open Curses does not mention that the cursor should be made invisible
       as a side-effect of lleeaavveeookk.  SVr4 curses documentation does this,  but
       the code does not.  Use ccuurrss__sseett to make the cursor invisible.

